<title>UK: Only Britain will reach EU jobs target - paper.</title>
<headline>Only Britain will reach EU jobs target - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain will probably be the only country to meet the European Union's target of cutting unemployment in half by 2000, the Times newspaper reported.</p>
<p>Citing an unpublished European Commission report, the newspaper said Britain could cut unemployment to 5.5 percent by the end of the century, from 10.5 percent at the beginning of the decade.</p>
<p>It quoted the report as saying there was little evidence a moderate minimum wage, opposed by the ruling Conservative Party, would cost jobs.</p>
<p>It also said the government had done little to provide a more flexible labour market.</p>
</text>
